      {
        "id": 238850,
        "name": "doppelgangerung",
        "username": "doppelgangerung",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/doppelgangerung/{size}/1876_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-06-30T00:57:43.079Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Heck of a fight! <div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/3/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1\" title=\"Screenshot_20210629-190617\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1_2_219x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20210629-190617\" data-base62-sha1=\"7O5VZaQ6Cm6HgT6gkAckvFClq0x\" width=\"219\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1_2_219x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1_2_328x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1_2_438x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/3/36b8e70cdce0ae981e384aeffa47289c2b8e67e1_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20210629-190617</span><span class=\"informations\">1080×2460 599 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Mainstay lived up to his name in spades with Leader Of The Pack, Durasteel Studded Vest, and Shard Strength, and with frequent assistance from Writhe’s MkII Shadow Projector.</p>\n<p>Blade’s Impulsion Beam was in tight competition with Miss Information for top of my aggro list - after that it was a matter of choosing whichever target was most vulnerable.</p>\n<p>The Citizens became Enemy Number One as soon as Bastion was replaced by Wildfire - without the damage reduction and resurrection capabilities provided by that card and Hammer And Shield, they fell pretty quickly.</p>\n<p>In the endgame, Lifeline played Cosmic Immolation with 3 hp left to bring down Plague Rat - and got away with it, thanks to Mainstay intercepting damage meant for him, Harpy went full bird-lady and burned her entire hand to take out Citizen Hammer with a Direct Strike, and Lifeline pulled out a Cryptic Alignment to deliver the final blow to the Baron!</p>\n<p>Edit: I misremembered a few details near the end -  an Immolation-boosted Cryptic Alignment finished off the Rat, but Chrono Ranger’s Compounded Bow delivered the final blow to Blade.</p>",
